      "local_reason_code": "cloud_message_bus_dlq_not_applicable",
      "local_deviation": "The Cloud message-bus DLQ has no Local equivalent. Local retry and recovery remain owned by their specific sidecar outbox contracts rather than a fabricated global queue.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Cloud Desktop now mounts a native global-admin Dead Letter Queue route with strict Cloud DTO validation, separate message and statistics loading/error/retry states, empty and stale preservation, status/event/error/routing filters, pagination, manual and visible-tab 30-second refresh, authoritative detail reads, single and batch retry, reason-required single and batch discard, cleanup confirmation, conflict and forbidden handling, and scope-aware cancellation. The renderer advertises only actions granted by the capability snapshot and route entry remains gated by the structured global_admin permission. Local does not call Cloud APIs and retains the stable cloud_message_bus_dlq_not_applicable disposition because retry and recovery remain owned by their specific sidecar outbox contracts."
    }
